From: Spaceghost <spaceghost@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spl: skip unused export-table population

SPL has no standalone application jump table. Avoid expanding the full U-Boot
export list there, where malloc is intentionally mapped to malloc_simple and
would also rewrite the jump-table field name.

---
 common/exports.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/common/exports.c b/common/exports.c
index e8bcae4..d4f4662 100644
--- a/common/exports.c
+++ b/common/exports.c
@@ -27,4 +27,8 @@ void jumptable_init(void)
 {
 	gd->jt = malloc(sizeof(struct jt_funcs));
+#ifdef CONFIG_SPL_BUILD
+#undef EXPORT_FUNC
+#define EXPORT_FUNC(f, a, x, ...)
+#endif
 #include <_exports.h>
 }
-- 
